WEBVTT

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.550
Evolution is Impossible!

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.550
Digivice Breakdown

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:07.780
Evolution is Impossible!

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:09.530
Digivice Breakdown!

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:13.300
In order to stop Kurata and his plans of Digimon genocide,

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:19.540
Masaru and the others headed to the Digital World using the Digital Gate opened up by Professor Noguchi.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:25.560
En route, they encountered Kouki, Nanami, and Ivan, a team of Kurata's henchmen.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:33.820
What's more surprising, these three transformed into Digimon and completely overpowered our heroes.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:40.430
However, at the risk of their lives, Satsuma and Kudamon appeared to take on their attacks,

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:44.760
allowing Masaru and the others to successfully pass through the Digital Gate.

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:52.720
Are we near Jureimon's forest yet?

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:53.720
Almost there.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:57.620
But... I thought we were looking for that nasty Kurata.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:00.130
Why do we have to go see Jureimon?

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:02.300
Jureimon is the oldest and wisest in the forests.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.020
He might know something.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:08.650
This is terrible!

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.940
Just... what happened?

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:14.020
Mushmon?

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:17.650
Gizmon:XT!

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.750
What is that...?

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:29.100
I won't forgive them...

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:36.820
I won't forgive them!

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.640
Let's go, Falcomon!

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:40.650
Yeah!

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.590
Digisoul...

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:49.450
Full Charge!

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:53.910
Falcomon, evolve!

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:12.630
Yatagaramon!

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:16.230
Haguro!

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:20.430
NOTE: <i>Haguro</i> (羽黒), meaning Black Wing, refers to the Shinto legend of Mount Haguro, when an imperial prince who wandered lost within the mountain was guided to its peak by a three-legged crow. 

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.430
Yatagaramon!

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:25.640
It's gotten faster than before!

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:30.810
There are other Gizmon:XT around!

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.700
This is the worst!

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:35.700
Let's go, Agumon!

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:35.980
Yeah!

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:38.560
Digisoul...

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:38.560
Digisoul...

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.290
Full Charge!

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.290
Full Charge!

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:49.470
Lilamon!

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:51.530
MachGaogamon!

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:56.210
We'll protect the Digimon!

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.380
Beauty Slap!

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.580
Gaoga Tornado!

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:11.140
Ah, Aniki!

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:27.310
Lalamon!

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:27.310
Gaomon!

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:29.580
Aniki!

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:30.640
Gaomon!

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.610
I'm all right, Master.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.000
This is strange.

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:38.320
Not only is Kurata not around, but neither are his minions.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:41.510
Don't tell me that they're acting on their own without partners...

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:42.930
Yatagaramon!

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:45.390
Mikafutsu-no-kami!

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:56.310
They're not gone!

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:58.690
So they've also raised their defense.

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:04.200
Falcomon!

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.520
They're stronger than before.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:09.070
They must have been modified even further!

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:10.660
That doesn't mean we still can't fight back!

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:16.310
What's that?

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:17.730
That sound...

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.450
It sounds like a reed pipe...

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:36.100
Who are you?!

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:39.070
Just a banchou who's passing through...

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:41.020
NOTE: A <i>banchou</i>  (番長) is a boss fighter.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:41.020
BanchouLeomon!

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:52.050
BanchouLeomon

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:52.050
Ultimate Level

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.320
BanchouLeomon.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:47.840
An Ultimate Level Digimon who faithfully lives according to the justice he believes in.

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:50.130
His special attack is Flash Banchou Punch.

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:52.050
His sharpened fighting spirit will knock you flat!

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:54.620
BanchouLeomon...

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.320
There's no record of him in DATS's database.

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:59.390
I've never seen him before either...

00:05:59.390 --> 00:06:01.020
Could he be a member of Kurata's troops?

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:03.320
No, that can't be.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:10.020
There's no evil in a guy that's a banchou!

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.580
Flash Banchou...

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:23.910
Punch!

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:31.130
Holy am I alone...

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:33.040
NOTE: This saying alludes to his high self-esteem. According to legend, Buddha was quoted to shout this after his birth.

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:33.040
throughout heaven and earth!

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:39.080
With my fists...

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.590
nothing is impossible!

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:47.200
Amazing...

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:50.950
He defeated all of those Gizmon:XT with just his fists!

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:53.990
Not bad, BanchouLeomon!

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:59.040
Want to try taking on these fists?

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:02.000
Interesting.

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:12.010
This guy...

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:15.550
He has no gaps in his form!

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:22.640
You're one million and 35 years too early to clash fists with me.

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:23.560
What?!

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:27.280
There's a critical difference between me and you.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:31.020
I have something right now that you guys don't.

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:32.450
Know what that is?

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.530
What you guys are lacking...

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:36.950
is power!

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:38.540
Power...

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:44.360
If it's power you want, I've got it right here.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:46.210
In my burning fists!

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:48.630
Simple fool.

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:50.550
Your fists aren't the only things that make up strength.

00:07:50.930 --> 00:07:51.800
What?

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:55.260
The answer lies within yourselves.

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:57.290
Within us?

00:07:57.290 --> 00:07:58.220
What's that mean?

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:01.470
Hey, wait a second!

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:04.180
Look for power!

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:06.580
Then convince me to acknowledge your strength!

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:09.940
When that time comes, I will allow you to fight me!

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:13.750
BanchouLeomon!

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:16.870
Damn, he just says whatever he wants and leaves...

00:08:17.500 --> 00:08:20.380
But he's right.

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:23.130
It's true that our strength is greatly inadequate right now.

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:28.050
We can't even begin to find a trace of Kurata anywhere if the Gizmon:XT keep delaying us...

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:31.700
But power isn't something that easy to attain...

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:32.900
Power...

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:35.020
Falcomon, let's go!

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:37.050
What's wrong, Ikuto?

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:39.560
There's a place where you can go to get power.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:40.390
Where?

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:42.240
I make sure to catch up with you later.

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:44.670
You guys go to Jureimon.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:45.920
Let's go, Falcomon!

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.600
Wait for me, Ikuto!

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:50.450
Hey, don't just run off!

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:52.250
You're messing up our teamwork!

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:53.320
You're one to talk.

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:57.050
Ikuto grew up in the Digital World.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:58.780
He must have an idea.

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:03.110
There's no doubt he's working hard to make up for Mercurimon's death.

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:05.500
Come on, let's hurry to Jureimon.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:06.930
Ah, yeah!

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:11.840
I've finally finished killing all of the Digimon in this village.

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:15.160
The Digimon's life energy...

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:17.540
I've collected quite a lot of it.

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:19.520
But it's still not enough.

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:21.400
Let's head to the next village.

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:22.670
Reporting in.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:29.020
We've lost all contact with the Gizmon:XT from the 13th Squad that were heading for Field 011.

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:30.460
What should we do?

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:33.480
That's odd news.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:36.110
Aniki, is this the place?

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:37.400
Um, yeah.

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:38.990
It should be around here.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:43.310
We need to catch Kurata quickly, before there are more victims.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:44.310
Yeah.

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:46.940
But this is the man who exploded DATS HQ to get what he wanted.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:49.810
We don't know what kind of foul traps he'll have set up for us.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:51.880
Besides, if we don't win...

00:09:52.310 --> 00:09:56.480
Kurata must have a considerable number of Gizmon:XT with him.

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:58.790
It will be difficult to battle, considering their numbers.

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:01.850
I guess this matter can't be settled through normal planning...

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:05.150
Who was that BanchouLeomon?

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:06.020
I dunno.

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:08.100
But his strength was the real thing.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:10.010
He's terribly strong.

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:11.060
Power, huh...?

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:11.060
Power, huh...?

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:17.090
Master!

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:19.030
Yoshino!

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:22.240
Hey Agumon, watch where you're going!

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:23.510
Not my fault!

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.870
 I can't even see my feet in this fog!

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:29.600
Get out!

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.040
Intruding humans!

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:35.590
Get out of here!

00:10:35.590 --> 00:10:36.590
Jureimon!

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:38.660
It's me, Masaru!

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:40.570
Masaru?

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.100
The fog turned into a tunnel!

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:01.020
There are so many injured Digimon...

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:06.500
It's been a long time, young ones.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:07.600
Jureimon!

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:12.230
Mercurimon has done an unfortunate thing.

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:13.880
So you knew...

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:16.980
The wind told me...

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:19.590
about the death of that heroic warrior.

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:21.770
It was immediately afterwards

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:28.350
when the Digimon who came from the human world began to obliterate the Digimon here.

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:31.670
It was the Gizmon that hurt these guys?!

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:37.100
That's why you covered the forest in fog, so you could protect those who were hurt.

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:41.360
But I couldn't rescue all of them.

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:46.600
The Digimon who they killed...

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:51.240
have died without being able to turn back into a Digiegg.

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:52.790
It is a sorrowful tale.

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:59.240
It looked like they were sucking the Digimon's life energy from them.

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:01.030
Why would they do that?

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:04.200
The Digimon's life energy?

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:05.390
I don't know.

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:08.640
But I have a bad feeling about it. A very bad feeling.

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:11.130
A guy named Kurata is behind all of this.

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:12.960
Do you know where he could be?

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:14.840
I don't know that either.

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:19.020
The only thing I'm certain of is that they are the ones attacking the Digimon.

00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:21.030
Even now, from places far away...

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:23.650
I can hear the screams the wind carries to me.

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:24.610
Damn Kurata...

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:27.070
Just wait until I punch him to the ground!

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:30.160
We have uninvited guests.

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:31.250
Guests?

00:12:35.590 --> 00:12:36.500
My, my.

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:42.140
We came here to find out why a team of Gizmon:XT were wiped out...

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:45.010
but to think we'd come upon such an interesting place.

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:46.720
That voice...

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:51.640
You!

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:54.600
So we meet again.

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:57.060
Where's Captain Satsuma?!

00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:59.280
Huh? Captain?

00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:01.270
Oh, you mean that old guy.

00:13:01.270 --> 00:13:02.030
He's dead.

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:04.490
The Captain is...?

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:06.260
Dead...?

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:11.770
I thought the orders we received would be quite boring to fulfill...

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:14.120
but I'm glad we ended up finding a playmate.

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:18.030
I like how vivacious she appears.

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:21.080
Maybe next time, I'll ask her out to dinner at a restaurant with a great view...

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:22.900
No, thank you.

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:27.070
How did she know what I was thinking about?

00:13:27.070 --> 00:13:29.990
I keep telling you, we can hear everything.

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:30.850
Anyway...

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:36.140
if we kill these Digimon here, I'm sure Kurata-chan will be satisfied.

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:43.010
You bastard...

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:48.700
That's the spirit!

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:08.130
Hyper Bio Evolution!

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:08.130
Hyper Bio Evolution!

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:16.100
BioThunderBirmon!

00:14:20.590 --> 00:14:22.110
BioCoatlmon!

00:14:26.620 --> 00:14:28.070
BioStegomon!

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.450
Digisoul...

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.450
Digisoul...

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:35.670
Full Charge!

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:35.670
Full Charge!

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:39.770
Agumon, evolve!

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:50.970
RiseGreymon!

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:53.270
Lalamon, evolve!

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:06.900
Lilamon!

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:08.690
Gaomon, evolve!

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:21.040
MachGaogamon!

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:24.790
Time to take revenge for the Captain!

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:26.030
RiseGreymon!

00:15:26.850 --> 00:15:28.520
Trident Revolver!

00:15:32.270 --> 00:15:33.730
Winning Knuckle!

00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:36.090
Beauty Slap!

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:45.090
What?

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:48.060
I've told you before!

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:51.060
Your attacks don't work on us!

00:15:51.060 --> 00:15:52.600
Thunder Storm!

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:55.110
RiseGreymon!

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:58.120
I've already figured out your attack pattern.

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:02.430
MachGaogamon!

00:16:03.050 --> 00:16:05.580
Accept this man's pure-hearted attack!

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:10.020
Lilamon!

00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:16.760
We can... still...

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:28.840
They're strong...

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:31.300
Far stronger than the Gizmon:XT!

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:32.270
Stop it...

00:16:32.270 --> 00:16:33.380
Stop it now!

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:34.480
You bird bastard!

00:16:34.710 --> 00:16:35.940
M-Masaru!

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:43.700
Masaru!

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:55.130
You're not even worthy enough to play with.

00:16:55.130 --> 00:16:57.640
A man's pure-hearted power is invincible.

00:16:57.950 --> 00:16:58.940
Little shits.

00:16:58.940 --> 00:17:03.100
You think you can defy us, when we're fused with both the powers of human and Digimon?

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:08.360
You got away because someone butted in last time...

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:10.480
But today, you're all dead!

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:11.730
RiseGreymon...!

00:17:14.730 --> 00:17:16.100
Nyokimon...!

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:18.490
Outta the way!

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:27.010
Jureimon!

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:30.710
Are you an idiot?

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:33.050
Trying to save these pieces of scum...

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:37.340
If you wanna die that badly, I'll give you what you wish for!

00:17:49.850 --> 00:17:52.390
You still have the strength to fight back?

00:17:55.600 --> 00:17:56.940
RiseGreymon!

00:18:00.520 --> 00:18:01.490
Aniki...!

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:09.670
Jureimon!

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:11.560
I've decided!

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:15.790
Your names in my autobiography will be Small Fries A, B, and C!

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:19.930
Jureimon!

00:18:22.340 --> 00:18:23.300
Jureimon!

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:32.370
C'mon!

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:34.990
Want to tell us any last words?

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:40.820
STOP IT!

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:40.820
STOP IT!

00:18:56.760 --> 00:18:57.830
What the hell?

00:18:58.870 --> 00:19:00.440
RiseGreymon...?

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:27.280
Whoa...

00:19:27.280 --> 00:19:28.940
What was that power?

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:35.440
Our Digivices...

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:39.590
That was a dirty trick, you bastards!

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:42.400
What the hell was that?

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:43.850
Huh?!

00:19:43.850 --> 00:19:45.220
I didn't hear of this!

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:48.140
We'll retreat for now. Open the Digital Gate!

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:50.640
You're dead for sure next time!

00:19:51.070 --> 00:19:51.930
What?

00:19:56.940 --> 00:19:59.110
H-Hey, hold it!

00:19:59.110 --> 00:19:59.960
Kurata!

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:00.990
Tell us where Kurata is!

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:07.820
I must do this to protect the Digimon who are injured.

00:20:07.820 --> 00:20:13.300
This wall I make will guard everyone as I sleep in order to restore myself.

00:20:13.300 --> 00:20:15.720
The future of the Digital World...

00:20:15.720 --> 00:20:19.230
I will entrust to you humans.

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:22.590
For that is Mercurimon's will...

00:20:23.900 --> 00:20:24.920
Agumon...

00:20:24.920 --> 00:20:27.850
If you had that power to begin with, you should've used it!

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:29.060
Don't be stingy.

00:20:29.060 --> 00:20:32.150
No, that was your power, Aniki.

00:20:32.150 --> 00:20:34.770
Your Digisoul made me stronger!

00:20:35.060 --> 00:20:36.930
My power?

00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:40.730
<i>The answer lies within yourselves.</i>

00:20:41.160 --> 00:20:45.950
He was talking about the power that was sleeping inside of me...

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:48.620
Anyway, what are we going to do with these?

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:52.570
From the damage they've received, they're impossible to repair.

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:54.300
I'm not surprised.

00:20:54.300 --> 00:20:58.080
That power we felt must have been the power of the Ultimate Level, which will take us beyond Perfect.

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:01.590
But our Digivices couldn't handle it.

00:21:02.300 --> 00:21:03.930
They couldn't handle it...

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:05.200
is not what I'm asking!

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:09.540
Now that we can't use our Digivices, we can't make our Digimon evolve!

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:11.560
How are we going to fight from now on?

00:21:12.440 --> 00:21:13.220
That's right!

00:21:13.220 --> 00:21:14.450
If we had Dad...!

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:17.000
Professor Daimon?

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:19.030
Dad made these Digivices!

00:21:19.030 --> 00:21:20.650
I'm sure he can fix them!

00:21:20.650 --> 00:21:26.490
But Professor Daimon has been missing in the Digital World for ten years!

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:28.260
So we'll find him!

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:30.370
Dad's definitely alive somewhere.

00:21:30.370 --> 00:21:32.260
Just you wait, Dad!

